---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
---

<GuideLayout slug="best-fortnite-landing-spots">
  <div class="gx-guide">
    <div class="gx-hero">
      <p class="gx-hero__kicker">Win the drop, not just the loot</p>
      <p class="gx-hero__line">
        Don't just drop where the loot is — drop somewhere you can <strong>rotate out of</strong>, land the
        <strong>high ground</strong> inside it, and cut your glider so you touch down <strong>first</strong>.
      </p>
      <div class="gx-glance">
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">🗺</span> Rotate-friendly spot</span>
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">⛰</span> Land high</span>
        <span class="gx-chip"><span class="gx-chip__i">🪂</span> Cut = land first</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="gx-intro">
      Picking where to drop is half of every Fortnite match — and most guides stop at "go where the loot
      is." The other half is <strong>getting there first</strong>, which comes down to timing and bus
      geometry. Here's how to nail both.
    </p>

    <h2>🎯 Choosing the spot: 3 trade-offs</h2>
    <div class="gx-steps">
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">1</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>Loot vs. fights</h3>
          <p>Named POIs have the best loot — and the most enemies. Drop one and you either win the early
            fight or die with nothing. Warming up or playing for placement? A quieter landmark on the edge of
            a POI gets you geared without the coin-flip.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">2</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>Think rotation, not just loot</h3>
          <p>A great spot you can't leave is a trap. Check where the early circles usually pull and whether
            you've got a clean way out — high ground, a vehicle, or a low-traffic path. Landing on the wrong
            side of the map quietly costs you the mid-game.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gx-step">
        <div class="gx-step__num">3</div>
        <div class="gx-step__body">
          <h3>Land high, then drop down</h3>
          <p>Inside a POI, grab the highest building or hill first. Height = first weapon, first shots, and
            the option to back off if it goes bad. Roll-land so you keep full HP.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>🪂 Getting there first: the part nobody calculates</h2>
    <p>
      Whoever lands first wins the fight before it starts. In the current glider-cut meta, that comes down
      to exactly where you jump and where you cut the glider — not holding forward and hoping. The solver
      uses the published movement constants for the current route:
    </p>
    <div class="gx-specs">
      <div class="gx-spec"><div class="gx-spec__v">~75 m/s</div><div class="gx-spec__l">Bus speed</div></div>
      <div class="gx-spec"><div class="gx-spec__v">832 m</div><div class="gx-spec__l">Bus altitude</div></div>
      <div class="gx-spec"><div class="gx-spec__v">100 m</div><div class="gx-spec__l">Glider auto-deploys</div></div>
    </div>
    <p>
      The fastest line: <strong>cut the glider</strong>, nosedive, and only glide at the very end. The cut
      point sits somewhere between the bus and your target — never right on top of either. Eyeballing it is
      guesswork, and being half a second late loses the fight.
    </p>

    <div class="gx-callout">
      <p class="gx-callout__tag">🧮 That's the whole reason we built Dropmaxxer</p>
      <p>
        Open <a href="https://dropmaxxer.pages.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dropmaxxer</a> and click
        <strong>Let's Drop</strong>. Use <strong>Set Bus</strong> to trace your battle-bus path, then
        <strong>Set Target</strong> and choose your POI. The Flight Plan gives you the fastest cut-and-dive
        line, the safe glide line, both ETAs, the exact spot to cut, and roll-land guidance. Turn on
        <strong>Pro Drops</strong> when you want to see where competitive players are landing this season.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="gx-outro">
      <strong>The play:</strong> pick a spot you can rotate out of, use Dropmaxxer to plan the line, land the
      high ground inside it, and cut your glider at the calculated point so you're the one holding a gun when
      the fight starts.
    </p>
  </div>
</GuideLayout>
